# Development Workflow Guidelines

## Local Development Setup
1. Install Ruby and Jekyll dependencies: `bundle install`
2. Install Node.js dependencies: `npm install`
3. Start local server: `bundle exec jekyll serve`
4. Access site at: `http://localhost:4000`

## File Structure Conventions
- **Layouts**: `_layouts/` - Page templates and structure
- **Includes**: `_includes/` - Reusable components and snippets
- **Styles**: `_sass/` - SCSS files for styling
- **Assets**: `assets/` - Images, CSS, JS, and other static files
- **Plugins**: `_plugins/` - Custom Jekyll plugins

## Key Layout Files
- [default.liquid](mdc:_layouts/default.liquid) - Base layout template
- [post.liquid](mdc:_layouts/post.liquid) - Blog post layout
- [page.liquid](mdc:_layouts/page.liquid) - Static page layout
- [about.liquid](mdc:_layouts/about.liquid) - About page layout

## Key Include Files
- [head.liquid](mdc:_includes/head.liquid) - HTML head section
- [header.liquid](mdc:_includes/header.liquid) - Site navigation
- [footer.liquid](mdc:_includes/footer.liquid) - Site footer
- [scripts.liquid](mdc:_includes/scripts.liquid) - JavaScript includes

## Content Management
- Use [optimize_seo.py](mdc:optimize_seo.py) for SEO optimization
- Follow the established front matter structure
- Maintain consistent file naming conventions
- Update both English and Chinese versions when applicable

## Build and Deployment
- Test locally before pushing changes
- Ensure all links work correctly
- Validate YAML front matter syntax
- Check for broken images or assets
- Deploy to GitHub Pages via main branch

## Customization Points
- Theme colors: Modify `_sass/_base.scss`
- Typography: Update `_sass/_base.scss` font settings
- Layout modifications: Edit layout files in `_layouts/`
- Component changes: Modify files in `_includes/`
